              {
                "id": "studio-founder-column-9",
                "type": "text",
                "values": {
                  "anchor": "",
                  "displayCondition": null,
                  "selectable": true,
                  "draggable": true,
                  "duplicatable": true,
                  "deletable": true,
                  "hideable": true,
                  "_meta": {
                    "htmlID": "u_content_text_3",
                    "htmlClassNames": "u_content_text"
                  },
                  "linkStyle": {
                    "inherit": true,
                    "linkColor": "#514293",
                    "linkHoverColor": "#514293",
                    "linkUnderline": true,
                    "linkHoverUnderline": true
                  },
                  "text": "A late-night comedy show used a clip of me this week. Be careful what you wish for!<br><br>The segment was about subscriptions, and they dug up an old interview where I talked about fridges that reorder milk by themselves. The host called it “mildly terrifying.” Fair.<br><br>Honestly? I’m a fan, so being teased on TV felt like an honour. It was a good rant: printers that stop working when a trial ends, cancel buttons hidden three menus deep, monthly fees for heated seats.<br><br>Jokes aside, it was strange to see an idea this community spent years working on turn up in a comedy monologue. We went from a small billing company to a topic people argue about at dinner. That doesn’t happen often.",
                  "fontSize": "17px",
                  "fontFamily": {
                    "label": "Helvetica",
                    "value": "helvetica,sans-serif"
                  },
                  "color": "#222222",
                  "textAlign": "left",
                  "lineHeight": "160%",
                  "containerPadding": "8px 56px"
                }
